## Semantic and temporal interpretation

- `game_id`: NBA identifier; normalize to a ten-character zero-padded string before joining.
- `game_date`: game-calendar date, not tipoff; values mix naive midnight ISO and midnight-with-Z encodings.
- `odds_date`: literal `open`, literal `close`, or a UTC timestamp for an odds update. The marker rows do not contain publication timestamps.
- `last_fetched`: retrospective scrape time (including 2026 for 2022 games), never a feature or an availability time.
- `decimal_home/away`: rounded quoted decimal prices; `moneyline_home/away`: signed American prices. Probability calculations convert American prices without decimal rounding.
- `source_url`: source provenance only. Home/away identity is cross-checked through NBA game identifiers and schedule metadata.
- Team boxscore counting and advanced columns describe the completed game, not pregame knowledge. Only strictly previous dates enter rolling features. `min` is elapsed game minutes (48 in regulation), unlike the NBA team-log total player minutes (240).
- All `*_rank`, `gp_rank`, `w_rank`, `l_rank`, `w_pct_rank`, `available_flag`, outcomes, and current-game quarter scores are excluded from predictors. Rank fields may encode retrospective context.
- Quarter columns `q1_*` through `q4_*` are regulation-quarter statistics. Quarter consistency is computed within prior completed games and then rolled forward; overtime is not treated as a fifth quarter.
- The player schema is inspected separately in feature construction, using selected columns and 50,000-row chunks. Only 2021–22 regular-season records through the backtest horizon are retained.
- Current-game movement, steam, update counts and TeamRankings close are diagnostic-only. Their historical team-side rolling values may enter a later game's features, with an explicit strictly-prior-date check.
